From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 10:32:09 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 247/297] Meridian: Ask with OpenCode 2.x runs on its own
 server

OpenCode 2.x run joins its background service when one is up; that service
never saw Meridian's config, so the agent was missing (Agent not found:
"meridian") and its deny-all didn't apply. Meridian now asks run --help and
passes --standalone where it exists (1.x doesn't know it). In the closed home
OpenCode can read the person's global opencode.json and opencode.jsonc, also
through a symlink and where XDG or OPENCODE_CONFIG_DIR moved them, and its own
folders exist before it starts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
